"name": "ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/riverwalk.webp", "description": "พื้นที่ตลาดริมแม่น้ำที่มีสินค้าและอาหารท้องถิ่น", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า/ถนนริมคลอง ข้างวัดย่านยาว", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.87157, "longitude": 98.35091}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เปิดให้เข้าชมเวลาใด", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · วันเสาร์ 15:00 ถึง 20:00 น."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีค่าเข้าชมหรือไม่", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · ไม่มีค่าธรรมเนียมการเข้าชม"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เดินทางไปย่านริมน้ำ/ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า บริเวณข้างวัดย่านยาว; แหล่งข้อมูลระบุว่าสามารถใช้รถรับจ้างท้องถิ่นหรือมอเตอร์ไซค์รับจ้างจากสถานีขนส่งตะกั่วป่าได้"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ตลาดมีชื่อในโครงการตลาดประชารัฐต้องชมว่า ‘ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า ร่วมใจประชารัฐ’ และตั้งอยู่ถนนริมคลองข้างวัดย่านยาว"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "มีแผงจำหน่ายขนมพื้นบ้าน อาหารพื้นเมือง สินค้าโอทอป และของดีเมืองตะกั่วป่า ตลาดตั้งอยู่ติดแนวคลอง/แม่น้ำตะกั่วป่า เหมาะกับการชมวิวริมน้ำและถ่ายภาพ รีวิวผู้ใช้ระบุว่ามีดนตรีสดโดยนักเรียนในบางช่วง"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/riverwalk/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/riverwalk/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Markets & Food</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Saved places · Markets and food</span><h1>Takuapa Riverwalk</h1><p class="english">Takuapa Riverwalk</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">9 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="riverwalk">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="eager"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.87157, 98.35091 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.87157,98.35091" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>Saturdays, 3:00 PM to 8:00 PM <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd>Free admission <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://www.dit.go.th/FILE/CONTENT_FILE/256202181736250948974.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#nearby-note"></a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From a mining town port to a riverside market space</h3><p class="era-years">No founding year has been found for the present market; old-town context: 1782 to the early 20th Buddhist century</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Available evidence describes the history of the Takua Pa town area and the pier, rather than specifying the exact origin of this riverside market. Takua Pa has been a port town and a centre for goods exchange since ancient times, before growing from tin mining and water trade. The old town is situated in a location surrounded by rivers on three sides, making it suitable for navigation, trade, and town defence.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai Community</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>When mining slowed, the pier became a memory and was then revived</h3><p class="era-years">Around the 1970s to 2019 (B.E. 2520 to 2562)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In the later period, the area was revitalised in the form of a community market under the name "Takuapa Riverwalk Ruamjai Pracharat". A Department of Internal Trade document with data as of 31 January 2019 (2562 BE) specified its location next to Wat Yan Yao (a local temple) and opening hours on Saturdays from 15:00 to 20:00. Evidence has not verified if the market was directly impacted by the 2004 tsunami or registered as a historical site under the market's name.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.dit.go.th/FILE/CONTENT_FILE/256202181736250948974.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A Saturday canal side market that brings old town memories back to life</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The market is located in the old town landscape featuring Chinese and Sino-Portuguese buildings. Riverside activities by the municipality still appear in planning documents, such as almsgiving along the river next to Wat Nikornwararam (Wat Yan Yao), and the Ministry of Culture lists a seafood festival specifying the market as the venue. However, the name of the agency or person directly managing the market has not been verified, nor have permanent restoration projects for the market itself in 2026.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gplace</a> · <a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thai-tour</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality: Development Plan Monitoring Report</a> · <a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม (Cultural Calendar, Ministry of Culture)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1809 (พ.ศ. 2352)</p><h3>Original town destroyed by the Burmese and people migrated</h3><p>The original Takua Pa town was destroyed and abandoned before being revived around Ban Talat Yai during the reign of King Rama III.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2018 (พ.ศ. 2561)</p><h3>Market listed in the Must-See Market project</h3><p>Government documents name the Takua Pa Riverside Market, Ruam Jai Pracharath in Phang Nga province.</p><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Information as of 31 January 2019 (พ.ศ. 2562)</p><h3>Official location and time data available</h3><p>The Department of Internal Trade states that the market is located on the canal-side road next to Wat Yan Yao and opens on Saturdays from 3:00 PM to 8:00 PM.</p><a href="https://www.dit.go.th/FILE/CONTENT_FILE/256202181736250948974.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Takua Pa grew into a port and trade center</h3><p>The riverside area was the axis for navigation, goods exchange, and settlements of people from various nations.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Chap Se area served as an old port</h3><p>The name Chap Se is a Hokkien Chinese word meaning port, and is associated with the Chinese merchant community and the tin mining economy.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Mines gradually closed, town shifted from a mining hub to an old town</h3><p>Local historical sources note that prosperity from mining declined after the mines gradually closed, and the river became shallow due to mining sediment.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Seafood festival uses the market as a venue</h3><p>The Ministry of Culture's cultural calendar lists the Takua Pa Seafood Festival at the riverside market, although accessible pages do not clearly show the event dates.</p><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><p class="muted">No images authorized for publication in this category yet</p></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Local food and snacks</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Stalls selling local sweets, native food, OTOP products, and Takua Pa's specialities.</p><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Canal side atmosphere</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The market is located along the Takua Pa canal or river, suitable for river viewing and photography.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Performances and music</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>User reviews indicate there is live music by students at times.</p><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Connecting to the old town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located near Takua Pa old town and the Sino-Portuguese buildings of the Talat Yai community.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The term "Chap Se" used for the old commercial district is related to a Hokkien Chinese word and the old Takua Pa pier.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Takua Pa old town has evidence of water trade with merchant ships from China and Myanmar.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Travel to the riverside area or Sri Takuapa Road near Wat Yan Yao. Sources suggest using local hired vehicles or motorcycle taxis from the Takua Pa bus terminal.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Wat Yan Yao (Wat Nikorn Wararam) <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.dit.go.th/FILE/CONTENT_FILE/256202181736250948974.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Takua Pa old town / Talat Yai community <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Takua Pa bus terminal <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">Stop nearby</span><p>If you want to sit and rest after walking through the market, the old market area is not far away. An old wooden house on Thanon Rat Bamrung is open as a café.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A place to sit near the market ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Not verified · Saturdays, 15:00 to 20:00</p></details><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · No admission fee</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Travel to the riverside area or Sri Takuapa Road near Wat Yan Yao. Sources suggest using local hired vehicles or motorcycle taxis from the Takua Pa bus terminal.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The market is named 'Takua Pa Riverside Market, Ruam Jai Pracharath' in the Must-See Pracharath Market project and is located on the canal-side road next to Wat Yan Yao.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Stalls sell local sweets, regional food, OTOP products, and goods from Takua Pa. The market sits beside the canal·Takua Pa River, making it suitable for riverside views and photography. User reviews say students sometimes perform live music.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.dit.go.th/FILE/CONTENT_FILE/256202181736250948974.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta (OpenStreetMap data)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thai-tour</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gplace</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai Community</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/index.php/site/detail/4431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wanderlog</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม (Cultural Calendar, Ministry of Culture)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ministry of Commerce: Must-See Markets in Southern Thailand</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Coordinates with a specific riverside market sign were not found, so market or nearby coordinates from OpenStreetMap via Mapcarta are used.</li><li>Phone number, Facebook page, website, or official LINE of the market not found.</li><li>Evidence confirming the founding year, creator, or historical site registration of the market not found.</li><li>Verified data on parking, restrooms, access for the elderly or wheelchairs, and dress code not found.</li><li>Festivals specific to the market not verified.</li><li>Official image links with specified usage rights are not verified.</li><li>Evidence specifying the first opening year, founder, responsible person, or owner agency of the market not found.</li><li>Evidence of the market being abandoned, restored, or changing hands during any period not found.</li><li>Evidence verifying direct impact from the 2004 tsunami on the market area not found.</li><li>Evidence of the riverside market being registered as a historical site not found; registrations found belong to other elements in the old town.</li><li>Latest market opening announcement for 2026 from direct caretakers not found, so current opening days and times cannot be verified yet.</li><li>News from the past 5 years specifying direct market restoration or development projects with clear publication dates not found.</li><li>Old photos identified directly as the riverside market area not found.</li><li>All photos are links from online travel sources with unknown rights, requiring permission before use.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\phra-narai\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Phra Narai Park · Takuapa attractions · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Rest in the park and continue with town history · Phra Narai Park Takuapa · Takua Pa park · Phang Nga cultural sites"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Phra Narai Park · Takuapa attractions"><meta property="og:description" content="Rest in the park and continue with town history · Phra Narai Park Takuapa · Takua Pa park · Phang Nga cultural sites"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/phra-narai.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/phra-narai.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/phra-narai/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์ ตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/phra-narai.webp", "description": "สวนในพื้นที่เทศบาลที่มีเรื่องราวเกี่ยวกับองค์พระนารายณ์", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "หมู่ชุมชนศรีเมือง ถนนเพชรเกษม", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8696046, "longitude": 98.3445279}, "telephone": "076 421 750"}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อยู่ตรงข้ามสำนักงานเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่าและที่ว่าการเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า บนถนนเพชรเกษม"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "สวนอยู่ภายใต้การดูแลบริหารจัดการของเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า สวนเป็นสถานที่พักผ่อนหย่อนใจและเป็นที่ประดิษฐานองค์เทวรูปพระนารายณ์กับเทพบริวารจำลอง"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ประติมากรรมรูปเคารพพระนารายณ์สำหรับให้ประชาชนสักการะบูชา ภายในสวนมีองค์พระนารายณ์และเทพบริวารจำลองตามข้อมูลแหล่งราชการ พื้นที่ส่วนหนึ่งของสวนจัดเป็นสนามเด็กเล่น"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/phra-narai/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/phra-narai/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Parks & Public Spaces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place notes · Parks and public spaces</span><h1>Phra Narai Park</h1><p class="english">Phra Narai Park</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">5 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="phra-narai">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/phra-narai.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8696046, 98.3445279 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8696046,98.3445279" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076 421 750 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact information ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>The park's origins remain behind a veil of evidence</h3><p class="era-years"></p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>For Phra Narai Public Park itself, no document has been found stating its construction year, initiator, or reason for establishment. It should therefore not be concluded that the park originated in the tin-mining era or during the period of the town governors merely because Takuapa prospered then.</p><p>What can be confirmed is that the park is in front of Takuapa Town Municipality Office and houses a statue of Phra Narai with replicas of attendant deities. Phra Narai is significant to the town and is used in the municipal emblem, but this evidence explains the significance of the deity and the town, not the park's founding date.</p><p>Takua Pa's context in municipal documents reflects an old town shaped by trade, tin mining, Sino-Portuguese buildings, and a large Chinese community. However, no evidence directly links these elements to the park's construction.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</a> · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a sacred space to a town activity stage</h3><p class="era-years">No verifiable timeline has been found.</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The evidence found does not record any transfer of ownership, abandonment, or restoration of the park over time, so it cannot yet be answered whether the park experienced these events. The same applies to the impact of the 2004 tsunami (B.E. 2547), for which no report specifically about this park has been found.</p><p>During the period covered by the available information, the park's role expanded from a place of worship to a public space for the town. It is used for cultural activities, recreation, traditional events, Children's Day events, and as a playground, under the management of Takuapa Town Municipality.</p><p>Old-town documents identify several places and ancient monuments in the municipality, but no Fine Arts Department announcement has been found registering “Phra Narai Park Public Garden” directly as an ancient monument. The park is therefore carefully distinguished from nearby ancient monuments.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A public park in the 2026 context</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The latest publicly available information confirms that the park remains a public space under the care of Takuapa Town Municipality. It contains statues of Phra Narai and attendant deities for worship, as well as a playground and community recreation areas.</p><p>The park also serves as the town's central stage. The Phra Narai worship ceremony and Takua Pa local-products event were held here in 2025 (B.E. 2568), with reports of Takua Pa local-products activities at the park's central stage. The 2023 (B.E. 2566) annual event ran from 27 March to 5 April.</p><p>No official information has been found confirming opening and closing hours, admission fees, the latest physical condition, or a completed construction project. For the proposed “Narai Hub &amp; Commercial Center”, only policy or guidance reports from municipal administrators have been found, so it is not yet considered a completed project.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath</a> · <a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ThaiPR.NET</a> · <a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Naewna</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">27 March to 5 April 2023 (B.E. 2566)</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony</h3><p>The annual event is held at Phra Narai Public Park, along with cultural activities and community products.</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2025 (2568 BE)</p><h3>Takua Pa good products fair</h3><p>The central stage of the community economic promotion project was held in the park.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Current status</h3><p>It remains a public park under the municipality's care. It features a worship point, a playground, and an event space.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>The year the park was built has not been found</h3><p>The disclosed documents do not specify the year, founder, or park establishment project.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Phra Narai statue as a city symbol</h3><p>The municipality document states that the Phra Narai statue is sacred to the townspeople and is used as the municipality seal, but does not specify the year it was enshrined in the park.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Phra Narai and attendant statues</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Replicas of the deities enshrined in the park. The originals are ancient sculptures from the Khao Phra Narai archaeological site, now in the Thalang National Museum.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Municipal symbol</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is used as the emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality, reflecting the town's historical roots linked to Indian culture.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Proximity to the Sunday Market</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The park is a landmark near the Takua Pa Old Town Sunday Market, often used as an activity space or gathering point for festivals.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Event area</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Used for municipal cultural activities, recreation, and local traditional events</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-03-14 · ThailandTravel</p><h3>Phra Narai Worship and Takua Pa Good Products Fair 2025 (2568 BE)</h3><p>Announced the event schedule for 14 to 23 March 2025 at the park.</p><a href="https://thailandtravel.app/content/read/3344" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2023-03-31 · ThaiPR.NET</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony, an identity of Takua Pa people</h3><p>Reported on the annual event in 2023 (2566 BE), which was held at the park between 27 March and 5 April.</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted"> · Siam Rath</p><h3>Takua Pa Town Municipality organised community economic promotion activities, Takua Pa good products</h3><p>Used the park's central stage as the area for the 2025 community economic promotion project.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai statues in the park are replicas; the original ancient sculptures were moved for safekeeping at the Thalang National Museum in Phuket.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is the official emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/thung-phra/">Thung Phra Pho Park</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The park is managed by Takuapa Town Municipality. It is a place for recreation and houses statues of Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>A Phra Narai devotional sculpture is available for public worship. According to official sources, the park contains Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities, and part of the park is a playground.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Cultural Information Centre (m-culture)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AAาธารณะอุทยานพระนารายณ์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Phang Nga Primary Educational Service Area Office</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ThaiPR.NET</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9550000099132" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Naewna</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Published and verified opening hours are not verified.</li><li>Admission fee data is not verified.</li><li>Current conditions of facilities like restrooms, parking, and wheelchair accessibility are not verified for 2026.</li><li>The specific schedule for the annual Phra Narai worship ceremony is not confirmed.</li><li>Verified distance from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>No information on the construction year or builder has been found.</li><li>No evidence confirming the park's role during the tin-mining era has been found.</li><li>No evidence was found confirming Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architecture at the garden</li><li>No evidence was found that the garden is registered as an ancient monument</li><li>No nearby places with a verified walking distance were found</li><li>No verified event month or lunar calendar information was found</li><li>The garden's construction year and builder</li><li>The garden's original purpose or founding project</li><li>The history of ownership changes, abandonment, or restoration</li><li>Evidence of impact from the 2004 tsunami ( พ.ศ. 2547 )</li><li>The year the garden itself was registered as an ancient monument</li><li>Opening and closing hours, admission fees, and the latest condition of buildings and structures</li><li>Whether the Narai Hub project is actually underway</li><li>No old image explicitly identified as showing the garden has been found</li><li>No direct URL for a current image file with verifiable usage rights has been found</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="