://takuapa101.com/places/rong-jae/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/rong-jae/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Shrines & Vegetarian Halls</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Shrines and vegetarian halls</span><h1>The Shrine in the Garden</h1><p class="english">The Shrine in the Garden</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">6 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="rong-jae">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/rong-jae.webp" alt="โรงเจในสวน" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://roijang.com/phangnga/โกสุ้ย-ขนมพื้นเมือ-งตะกั่วป่า-พังงา-2023-12-6/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>An old shrine of the Chinese community in Takua Pa</h3><p class="era-years">The exact construction year is unknown; municipal documents state that it is more than a century old</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Rong Jae Nai Suan, or Seng Leng Keng Shrine, appears in Takua Pa Town Municipality documents as a centuries-old shrine, but the same documents do not give its construction year. It is therefore not yet possible to place its beginnings in a particular reign.</p><p>The founder identified in municipal documents is Mr So Thian Seng, an overseas Chinese settler. After the shrine was completed, Phra Cheng Chui Cho Sue, or Chao Pho Yat Nam Khang, was brought from China and enshrined there. The place therefore likely served both as a site of worship and as a centre of belief for the Chinese community in the mining and port town of Takua Pa. However, there is no site-specific evidence for its construction year, the founder's policy rationale, or its everyday role at the time.</p><p>Another local document says that Mr So Seng had worked with Ku Chai Tung Shrine before opening the shrine in the garden. However, it cannot yet be confirmed that he was the same person as Mr So Thian Seng, so these are not presented as the same fact.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</a> · <a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Vegetarian Festival, สภาวัฒนธรรมตำบลตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Sub-district Cultural Council)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>A transition period with blank documents</h3><p class="era-years">No confirmed year or event has been found</p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>Among the verifiable sources, no evidence has been found that the shrine changed ownership, was abandoned, or was restored in any particular year. No site-specific evidence has been found showing how the 2004 tsunami (พ.ศ. 2547) affected this building.</p><p>No historic-site registration entry has been found for Rong Jae Nai Suan, and there is no information that it was converted to another business or type of public building. The verifiable information for the intervening period is therefore limited to the continuity of the place name and memories of an old shrine. The history of another shrine in the old town should not be used to fill the gaps.</p><p>Takua Pa's context changed from a mining and maritime-trading town into a historic and cultural town, but the sources found do not yet connect this city-level change with specific events at Rong Jae Nai Suan.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>Still named in the Vegetarian Festival landscape, but operational status is unclear</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>Currently, verifiable online sources do not confirm who manages the shrine, whether it is open to visitors every day, what condition the building is in, or whether any restoration project is under way. It should therefore not be described as an open tourist attraction or as a place that can be visited without an appointment.</p><p>The contemporary evidence found is a review article reporting the sale of ko sui sweets at Rong Jae Nai Suan during the Vegetarian Festival. This indicates that the place was still used for a community festival activity, but it is a blog report, not a shrine schedule announcement, and does not confirm that the activity is held every year.</p><p>Travellers should use the Soi Rong Phra, Thanon Rat Bamrung address as a starting point and check with local people or the municipality before travelling, because no verified coordinates, opening hours, telephone number, or official contact channel are available.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://roijang.com/phangnga/โกสุ้ย-ขนมพื้นเมือ-งตะกั่วป่า-พังงา-2023-12-6/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roi Jang: Ko Sui, Takua Pa local dessert</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality: Place Information Document</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Founding of the shrine</h3><p>The municipality document identified the founder as Mr. So Thian Seng, an overseas Chinese, but did not specify the founding year.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Inviting the deity from China</h3><p>After building the shrine, Phra Cheng Chui Cho Sue, or the Dewdrop God, was invited from China to be enshrined.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Kosui snack activity in the Vegetarian Festival</h3><p>A review article reported the selling of Kosui snacks at the Shrine in the Garden, but it is not an official announcement and it is not verified if it will be held every year.</p><a href="https://roijang.com/phangnga/โกสุ้ย-ขนมพื้นเมือ-งตะกั่วป่า-พังงา-2023-12-6/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Deity Cheng Chui Cho Sue</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The deity that the municipality states is enshrined in the shrine. Also known as the Dewdrop Deity, it has a history of being invited from China.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Ko Sui snacks during the Vegetarian Festival</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The Roi Jang blog reports that Grandma Tan Si Lun sells Ko Sui snacks at the Shrine in the Garden during the Vegetarian Festival. This is information from a blog that still needs to be verified for sales in the year of travel.</p><a href="https://roijang.com/phangnga/โกสุ้ย-ขนมพื้นเมือ-งตะกั่วป่า-พังงา-2023-12-6/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The name "Rong Chae Nai Suan" (Shrine in the Garden) is a common name for Seng Leng Keng Shrine, according to Takua Pa Town Municipality data.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Municipal documents mention a reputation for traditional Chinese healing. This is the history of the place's beliefs, not evidence of medical efficacy.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Takua Pa Town Municipality's environmental action plan documents say that Rong Jae Nai Suan is called Seng Leng Keng Shrine and is more than a century old, without specifying an exact construction year. The municipality identifies its founder as Mr So Thian Seng, an overseas Chinese settler.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The deity that the municipality says is enshrined at the shrine is also known as Chao Pho Yat Nam Khang and is said to have been brought from China. The Hroi Jang blog reports that Ama Tan Si Lun sells ko sui sweets at Rong Jae Nai Suan during the Vegetarian Festival. This is blog information, and sales in the year of travel still need to be checked.</p></details><details><summary>How the municipality document mentions this place</summary><p>A place that documents connect with Chinese traditions and cultural continuity</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Town Municipality · Environmental Action Plan for Fiscal Year 2020 (พ.ศ. 2563)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Vegetarian Festival, Takua Pa Subdistrict Cultural Council · Copy on AnyFlip</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Hroi Jang Phang Nga · Ko Sui, a local sweet from Takua Pa, Phang Nga</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://roijang.com/phangnga/โกสุ้ย-ขนมพื้นเมือ-งตะกั่วป่า-พังงา-2023-12-6/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Vegetarian Festival, สภาวัฒนธรรมตำบลตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Sub-district Cultural Council)</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Roi Jang: Ko Sui, Takua Pa local dessert</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://roijang.com/phangnga/โกสุ้ย-ขนมพื้นเมือ-งตะกั่วป่า-พังงา-2023-12-6/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>The English name is used according to the brief. No source confirming this as the official English name has been found yet; SEO keywords are suggestions for searching, not search volume data.</li><li>No coordinates that can verify its identity have been found from Google Maps, OpenStreetMap, Mapcarta, or Wikidata.</li><li>A Google Map embedded in the Roi Jang article shows the name Rong Than Shrine Hiap Thian Tai Te, Thung Yai Shrine, Phang Nga Province, which does not match the Shrine in the Garden, so the coordinates from that map are not used.</li><li>The address is only known as Soi Rong Phra, Rat Bamrung Road; no specific building number, subdistrict, and postal code confirmed for the location have been found.</li><li>No verified opening hours and admission fees have been found, so it is not assumed that it is open every day or free.</li><li>No verified phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account for the shrine has been found.</li><li>No direct travel information to the shrine from Takua Pa town center, Phuket, or Khao Lak, including distances and public transport, has been found.</li><li>No exact construction year or restoration year has been found. The phrase "century-old" is not enough to calculate the construction year.</li><li>No specific evidence regarding the role of the Shrine in the Garden in the tin mining business has been found.</li><li>No verifiable description of this building's architecture has been found, so it is not stated as Sino-Portuguese or detailed with Chinese decorations.</li><li>No ancient monument registration announcement specific to the Shrine in the Garden has been found.</li><li>Founder information in the book on AnyFlip uses the name So Seng, while the municipality uses So Thian Seng, and a connection between the individuals cannot yet be made.</li><li>Only two highlights with direct evidence to the location were found, and the snack item is seasonal data from a blog. Therefore, it is not filled up to 3-6 items without evidence.</li><li>No month and lunar calendar specific to this shrine have been found, nor the 2026 schedule.</li><li>No visiting duration, dress code, parking, restrooms, ramps, or accessibility information for the elderly and wheelchairs have been found.</li><li>No verified walking routes from the shrine to nearby places have been found.</li><li>No official image link verifying it is the Shrine in the Garden and whose image can be checked has been found.</li><li>The newly referenced municipal document is the Environmental Operations Plan for Fiscal Year 2020.</li><li>No verified construction year, restoration year, or founding date has been found.</li><li>No evidence of changing hands, abandonment, other uses, effects from the 2004 tsunami, or site-specific ancient monument registration has been found.</li><li>No current caretaker, opening hours, building condition, development projects, coordinates, phone number, and official contact channels have been found.</li><li>No old or current photos that verify the identity of the Shrine in the Garden from readable sources have been found.</li><li>No news from the past five years specific to the Shrine in the Garden has been found.</li><li>The context of the tin mining era, maritime trade, and the Chinese community of Takua Pa still has no evidence tying it directly to specific events at this location.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
